  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Oregon has $1.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Oregon has 9,391 awards and an average award size of $205K. Obligations are down 7.5% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a peak of $2.5B in FY23, followed by $2.4B in FY24, $2.1B in FY25, and $1.9B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Oregon with $1.1B in obligations. Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry by obligations at $593M. VIGOR MARINE LLC is the largest vendor with $577M in obligations. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date, so the FY26 totals reflect the portion of the fiscal year reported so far. This snapshot highlights which agencies, industries, and vendors command the largest shares of federal contracting obligations in Oregon right now.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 7.5% year over year. Fiscal trends show $1.8B in FY21, $1.9B in FY22, $2.5B in FY23, $2.4B in FY24, $2.1B in FY25, and $1.9B in FY26. The FY26 total is a fiscal year to date figure and therefore partial. Tracking the year-by-year totals highlights where spending expanded and contracted across the five-year span."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors lead federal spending in Oregon?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buying with $1.1B in obligations. The top industries are Ship Building and Repairing at $593M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $219M. The largest vendor is VIGOR MARINE LLC with $577M, followed by COLLINS ELBIT VISION SYSTEMS, LLC with $196M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Agriculture with $299M and the Department of Transportation with $141M."
      }
    ]
  },
